"Iteration 2 makes three general engine fixes. On the 13 scans the engine can run, broad family-macro line-F1 rises from 0.832 to **0.896** (best F1 lane on the same scans: 0.649), and per-bend correctness given CAD from 57/80 to **63/80**. G1 still fails, though only by construction: the synthetic regression tier (50 cases) passes gate for gate as in iteration 1. G2 still fails overall and G3 cannot be evaluated, because the G3 truth table is not frozen yet and 13 cases are still refused.\n\nThe snapshot was taken before any edit. All edits are in five files under `domains/production/engine/inspect/`; `eval/` and `compile/` are untouched. Engine is now `e3-1.3.0`, config `417f580b\u2026`.\n\n**What changed, and why**\n1. **Free datum direction fixed by flange ends.** Two parts (49204020 and 15651004) had a datum whose edges and holes leave one in-plane direction undetermined, so six bend positions and lines were withheld. A CAD check of all 17 A1 parts confirmed these are the only two such parts.\n   - The fix uses the cut ends of flanges whose bend axes all run parallel to that direction. No bend moves those ends along it, formed or flat.\n   - It moves only the free direction and needs at least two ends that agree; the datum's own fixed directions never move.\n   - All six positions are now measured and pass (+0.22 to \u22120.14 mm), and 49204020 is fully in tolerance.\n2. **Joggles and short steps.** A CAD scan showed 10839000 has two 35\u00b0+35\u00b0 joggles with a 3.6 mm riser. 10839000 is a Gold11 family, has three of the refused staged scans, and is the real part in the end-to-end test.\n   - On a synthetic copy, the iteration-1 engine read the joggles as not formed. On the same-direction variant it gave four false FAILs.\n   - The fix narrows the hinge search near flat, requires a flat line to be continuous from the hinge, and stops a short child from growing onto the flange beyond it.\n3. **Metrology on short sides.** Station fits no longer run past the next bend's tangent line. A bend whose stations disagree with its panel planes by more than 10\u00b0 is now UNKNOWN instead of a confident wrong value.\n   - Synthetic probes, before \u2192 after: correct states 5/15 \u2192 13/15, false FAILs 4 \u2192 0.\n\n**Measured results** (frozen scorer)\n\n| Measure | Iteration 1 | Iteration 2 | Best F1 lane |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Broad, all 26 cases, family-macro / micro | 0.626 / 0.569 | **0.667 / 0.607** | 0.543 / 0.508 |\n| Broad, 13 runnable scans, family-macro / micro | 0.832 / 0.816 | **0.896 / 0.861** | 0.649 / 0.620 |\n| Gold set v1, 13 scans | 0.961 | **1.000** (80/80, 0 false lines) | 0.597 |\n| Per-bend correct, vs broad gold / vs any gold | 57 / 69 of 80 | **63 / 75 of 80** | \u2014 |\n| PASS on a bend with no published line | 6 | **0** | \u2014 |\n\n- G2(a) is unchanged: Gold11 relabel 0.574 over all 9 cases, 1.000 on the 4 that run.\n- No bend state changed on the real scans. The only decision changes are the six recovered positions and 11979003 B2's angle (PASS \u2192 REVIEW, by 0.007\u00b0).\n- The 38172000 angle FAILs are real scan geometry, not an engine error. Independent plane fits reproduce them within about 0.2\u00b0, so nothing was changed there.\n\n**Tests:** the new `tests/test_prod_engine_inspect_a1_iter2.py` passes 13/13; the E3 CLI suite 32/32; the earlier unit files 55/55. I changed one existing CLI test: it now marks every panel's free edges unusable, not just the datum's. Otherwise the new flange-end logic would correctly resolve the pose that test needs to stay undetermined; its assertions are unchanged.\n\n**Open and risks**\n- A joggle whose riser is shortened by a bend-line defect (to about 1 mm of flat) is still read as not formed. It gets no FAIL; fixing it needs a model that fits both bend angles and the riser length together.\n- The flat search window is now 0.4 mm (was 3 mm), and the joggle rules have not been seen on real staged scans. Both need checking on 10839000 and 23553000 once the G3 table is frozen.\n- Flange-end registration assumes the flange ends were cut straight along the bend axis.\n- Freezing the G3 truth table so the 13 refused cases can run is still the biggest lever.\n\nEverything is in `/Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/docs/production/runlog/a1/iter_2/`:\n- `CHANGE.md`\n- `engine_before.tgz`\n- `engine.diff`\n- `raw/`\n- `overlays/`\n- `diag/`\n- `tools/`"